IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qld-part04-references`

-- Tests for Part 4 (qld-part04-references.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 4`

#ASSERT `the Act may be referred to by the word Act alone (s 14E)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act may be referred to by the word Act alone (s 14E)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 14F`

#ASSERT `an Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(1))` `by its short title` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(1))` `by reference to the year in which it was passed and its number` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(1))` `in another way` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Examples 1 to 4 of citations.  Example 1 (a Statutory Instruments Act 1992 citation by short title) is limb (a);
-- examples 3 and 4 (Act No. 22 of 1992; 1992 Act No. 22) are limb (b).  Example 2 gives the short title with the number.
-- FORK example 2 (short title and number together): read as a citation by short title, limb (a) || read as a citation by year and number, limb (b)
-- src:150 | Examples of citations—
-- src:151 | 1 Statutory Instruments Act 1992
-- src:152 | 2 Statutory Instruments Act 1992, No. 22
-- src:153 | 3 Act No. 22 of 1992
-- src:154 | 4 1992 Act No. 22
@ref s 14F(1), examples 1 to 4 (src:150-154)
#ASSERT `an Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(1))` `by its short title` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(1))` `by reference to the year in which it was passed and its number` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (2): a Commonwealth Act, cited by its short title together with a reference to the Commonwealth.
#ASSERT `a Commonwealth Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a Commonwealth Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a Commonwealth Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act of another State or a Territory may be cited in the way (s 14F(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act of another State or a Territory may be cited in the way (s 14F(3))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): a British Act, together with a reference to the United Kingdom or the term UK, Imperial Act or Imp.
#ASSERT `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` TRUE `the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` TRUE `the term UK` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` TRUE `the term Imperial Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` TRUE `the term Imp` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` TRUE `no such reference` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` FALSE `the term UK` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 14G`

#ASSERT `an enactment may be cited by reference to the provision of the Act in which it is contained (s 14G(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an enactment may be cited by reference to the provision of the Act in which it is contained (s 14G(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference is made according to a copy the section names (s 14G(2))` `an official copy of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is made according to a copy the section names (s 14G(2))` `an official copy of the Act as amended` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is made according to a copy the section names (s 14G(2))` `any other copy` EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS In s 14G, Act includes a Commonwealth Act, an Act of another State, a Territory Act and a British Act; the list is open, so the text does not say that any other kind is not an Act (s 14G(3)).
#ASSERT `the kind is an Act in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition Act)` `a Commonwealth Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind is an Act in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition Act)` `an Act of another State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind is an Act in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition Act)` `a Territory Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind is an Act in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition Act)` `a British Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind is an Act in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition Act)` `anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the thing is an enactment in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition enactment)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the thing is an enactment in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition enactment)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a copy of an Act of Queensland or of an Act of Queensland as amended is an official copy (s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a copy of an Act of Queensland or of an Act of Queensland as amended is an official copy (s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (a))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph (b) uses "means": outside the presumption the copy is not an official copy.
#ASSERT `a copy of an Act of another jurisdiction or of such an Act as amended is an official copy (s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a copy of an Act of another jurisdiction or of such an Act as amended is an official copy (s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (b))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 14H`

-- SAYS A reference to a law includes the law as originally made and as amended; the remade version is included only if the law has been repealed and remade since the reference was made (s 14H(1)).
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the law as originally made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the law as amended from time to time since it was originally made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the law as remade` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the law as remade` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the law as remade, and as amended from time to time since it was remade` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the other law as in force when the provision was remade` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the other law as in force when the provision was remade` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `the other law as in force when the provision was remade, and as amended from time to time since the provision was remade` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` `any other version` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(2))` `the law as originally made` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(2))` `the law as remade` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(2))` `the law as remade` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(2))` `the other law as in force when the provision was remade` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the kind is a law in s 14H (s 14H(3), definition law)` `a Commonwealth Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind is a law in s 14H (s 14H(3), definition law)` `an Act of Queensland` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `make includes enact (s 14H(3), definition make)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `make includes enact (s 14H(3), definition make)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 14I and 14J`

#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to the short title or citation includes a reference to the short title or citation as amended (s 14I(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to the short title or citation includes a reference to the short title or citation as amended (s 14I(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the kind is a law in s 14I (s 14I(2), definition law)` `a Territory Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind is a law in s 14J (s 14J(2), definition law)` `an Act of another State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- SAYS A reference to a law as repealed or expired is a reference to the law as in force immediately before it was repealed or expired, so the 'repealed ABC Act 1950' is the ABC Act 1950 as then in force (s 14J(1) and its example).
#ASSERT `the state of the other law to which a reference to a repealed or expired law is (s 14J(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the other law as in force immediately before it was repealed or expired`
#ASSERT `the state of the other law to which a reference to a repealed or expired law is (s 14J(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
